**Issue**: Race condition - Object URLs might be revoked while still in use by LazyImage components
**Severity**: High
**Impact**: Components displaying revoked URLs will show broken images

**Scenario**: 
- T1: LazyImage A starts loading image.jpg
- T2: MediaCache creates blob:url-123 for image.jpg  
- T3: LazyImage A receives blob:url-123 and renders
- T4: User scrolls quickly, cache cleanup runs
- T5: Cache calls URL.revokeObjectURL(blob:url-123)
- T6: LazyImage A still visible but now shows broken image

**Suggestion**: Track URL usage by components:
```typescript
// In LazyImage.vue
onUnmounted(() => {
  if (cachedSrc.value?.startsWith('blob:')) {
    mediaCacheService.releaseUrl(src)
  }
})

// In mediaCacheService.ts
private urlRefCount = new Map<string, number>()

releaseUrl(src: string) {
  const entry = this.cache.get(src)
  if (entry?.objectUrl) {
    const count = (this.urlRefCount.get(entry.objectUrl) || 1) - 1
    if (count <= 0) {
      URL.revokeObjectURL(entry.objectUrl)
      this.urlRefCount.delete(entry.objectUrl)
    } else {
      this.urlRefCount.set(entry.objectUrl, count)
    }
  }
}
```

